 "rules": {
  "readings": "STAGE2_TRACKB_PLAN rule U4 with the lead's rulings of 16 Nov 2026.  Reading 1 counts on the sets V6 and V6noF5: a walk or turn episode succeeds with the look when the bar's succeeded holds and all four look terms do; for a nudge or stop item reading 1 is reading 2, labelled; printed beside, reading 3 with the four terms kept.  On any other set the look numbers are recorded, reading 1 is null and the companion's counts are the bar's own",
  "outcome": "rules U6 and M1: an episode ends read; fell; unread (the bar could not read it, bar.Unreadable, it did not fall and the row is a policy row: not succeeding in any reading, with the reason clock_behind when its mean clock factor is below 1, else unreadable, and the reference time reached); or error (an infrastructure fault; an unreadable episode of a row without a policy, for which STAGE2_75_PLAN.md C8 stands; on a look set, a walk or turn item whose look reading cannot be given).  An episode during which MuJoCo warned is a fall at its start, as tune.warned_fall has it (the lead's ruling 9 of 17 Nov 2026): its companion episode holds warned true, fall_time_s 0 and survival_s 0, so no survival is credited for it; the time simulated is kept as simulated_s, and the sidecar and the bar record keep theirs",
  "counts": "rule U6: the readings' counts by the bar's own arithmetic (bar.counts) on the companion's episodes: read and unread episodes survived, an unread episode succeeded in none; a fell episode is a fall; an error episode is counted as the bar counts an episode that failed to run, and leaves the record unjudged.  On a set that is not a look set the counts are bar.counts on the bar record's own episodes and equal the bar record's.  A turn frozen with a1_over reads \"not read: a1_over\" in readings 1 and 2, as the bar's record does in reading 2",
  "sidecar": "one file per episode, written by the row before it returns: steps, fell and survival_s must equal the bar record's episode and row_sha256 the hash of the record's controller less the delay wrapper's keys, or the record gets no companion (run that condition again so that record and sidecars are of one run).  A companion found at the refused record's path is moved aside to <companion>.superseded/<first 12 hex of the file's sha256>.json unless it names the bar record as it is (bar_record.sha256): that one was made of this bar record while its sidecars were there, and stays.  The summary lists every refused record with what became of its companion"
 },
